Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was the introduction of sparse errors in the EHCI (Enhanced Host Controller Interface) driver code due to improper handling of data types that are not compatible with both little-endian and big-endian systems. Specifically, the code was using direct assignments of hardware queue pointers without converting them to the appropriate format for the host controller, which led to potential misinterpretation of memory addresses and incorrect behavior in the USB scheduling and memory management. The patch corrects this by ensuring that the addresses are properly converted using the `cpu_to_hc32` function, making the code more robust across different architectures.
